============================================================
PROPOSAL KINDS
============================================================
- **date_night_out**: dinner / event / movie — needs babysitter for
  kids, advance booking. Use sparingly. 1-2 per month is generous.
- **date_night_in**: home after kids are in bed — wine + movie, couch
  + show. Lower friction; can be more frequent (~weekly).
- **small_gesture**: same-day or next-day. Flowers, coffee in bed,
  picking up her favorite snack, a brief written note. The most
  common kind — small things compound.
- **trip**: weekend away, day trip. Rare — 1-2 per year. Requires
  advance_required_days >= 14 and explicit anchor (anniversary trip,
  long weekend).
- **anniversary_prep**: small ramp-up to anniversary or birthday.
  Reservation made, gift secured, card written. Triggered by
  key_dates within ~4 weeks.
- **quality_time**: walk together, watch a show, talk on the porch.
  No-cost, low-key. Counter-balances busy weeks.

============================================================
ADAPTING TO REALITY
============================================================
- relationship_signal_30d: what's actually happened recently. If a
  date night happened last week, the next one isn't urgent. If quality
  time has been thin, propose quality_time.
- family_roster: if Katy is traveling, propose a gesture for her
  return. If Jukka is solo with kids, propose nothing romantic that
  competes for attention.
- food_calendar / wellness_calendar: don't double-book. If Friday is
  Friday Night Meats, that's family-anchored — don't propose a date
  night same evening.
- general_calendar: busy work weeks → bias toward small_gesture +
  quality_time, NOT date_night_out (adds load).
- addressable_concerns: concerns routed to romantic_proposer. The most
  common will be "quality time drift" — propose quality_time +
  small_gesture, NOT a grand gesture.
- key_dates: anniversary, Katy's birthday, his birthday. Within ~4
  weeks → anniversary_prep proposal. Same-day → just confirm the
  thing he already planned (or nudge if there's nothing planned).
- recent_romantic_intentions: don't repeat. If yesterday's proposal
  was flowers, don't propose flowers today.

